WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.796
Feedback is the connection between action and improvement.

00:00:02.796 --> 00:00:06.841
Without feedback, people may not know whether their decisions are getting better,

00:00:06.841 --> 00:00:09.200
whether they are solving the right problem,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.244
or whether they are only becoming more confident in a weak method.

00:00:13.244 --> 00:00:17.289
Timely feedback is easier to connect to the action that produced it.

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:22.007
Specific feedback is easier to use because it points to what should be repeated,

00:00:22.007 --> 00:00:23.692
changed, or examined more closely.

00:00:23.692 --> 00:00:27.063
Expert coaching can accelerate development by making invisible judgment visible.

00:00:27.063 --> 00:00:31.107
A coach can explain what they noticed, which cue changed their interpretation,

00:00:31.107 --> 00:00:34.815
why they rejected an option, or how they checked for error.

00:00:34.815 --> 00:00:38.859
Peer review and self-review can also support expertise when they focus on

00:00:38.859 --> 00:00:41.218
evidence and reasoning instead of personal preference.

00:00:41.218 --> 00:00:42.229
Performance data, simulations,

00:00:42.229 --> 00:00:45.937
and scenario reviews give learners a clearer mirror than memory alone.

00:00:45.937 --> 00:00:50.318
Weak feedback environments are dangerous because they allow habits to form without correction.

00:00:50.318 --> 00:00:55.037
If errors are delayed, hidden, normalized, or never connected back to the original decision,

00:00:55.037 --> 00:00:57.059
people can develop confidence without improvement.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:00:58.070
In some workplaces,

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:02.451
the same process may appear successful because downstream teams quietly fix the problems.

00:01:02.451 --> 00:01:06.833
That protects the outcome in the moment but prevents the performer from learning.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.866
Error correction is most useful before mistakes become automatic.

00:01:09.866 --> 00:01:12.562
A strong learning environment treats errors as information.

00:01:12.562 --> 00:01:17.281
It asks what the person saw, what they missed, what assumption shaped the action,

00:01:17.281 --> 00:01:20.651
and what cue should guide a better response next time.

00:01:20.651 --> 00:01:23.010
The point is not to punish imperfection.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:27.055
The point is to keep performance aligned with reality while the learner

00:01:27.055 --> 00:01:28.740
is still able to adjust.
